From f02c3eb561a37e5ac7ba26d26819245d8e24a9aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rarun <rarun@ami.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 11:36:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] SPI aspeed smc Fix RDSFDP timing issue with DMA optimizations

spi: aspeed-smc: Fix SFDP signature corruption by routing RDSFDP to USER mode

When DMA write and low-clock optimizations are enabled via DTS flags
(fmc-spi-dma-write and low-spi-clk-write), the RDSFDP (0x5A) instruction
timing becomes unreliable in normal_mode. This causes the 8 dummy cycles
requirement (per JESD216 standard) to be violated, resulting in 1-byte
read offset corruption and SFDP signature validation failure (0x06504446
instead of 0x50444653).

Route RDSFDP commands specifically through aspeed_spi_read_user() which
provides conservative CPU-controlled timing that correctly implements the
JEDEC JESD216 timing requirements regardless of DMA configuration.

This fix:
- Maintains JESD216 standard compliance (opcode 0x5A, 3-byte address, 8 dummy cycles)
- Uses proven code path already employed by dirmap_read() fallback
- Only affects RDSFDP reads (one-time at boot, 256 bytes)
- Does not impact normal flash read/write performance

Fixes: w25q01jvq flash not detected on AST2600 EVB FMC with DMA optimizations

Signed-off-by: rarun <rarun@ami.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c b/drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c
index 834091a61ca0..40c258ae1e99 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-aspeed-smc.c
@@ -736,6 +736,18 @@ static int aspeed_spi_exec_op_normal_mode(struct spi_mem *mem,
 		op->addr.buswidth, op->dummy.nbytes, op->dummy.buswidth,
 		op->data.nbytes, op->data.buswidth);
 
+	/*
+	 * SFDP reads must use USER mode to avoid timing alignment issues
+	 * when DMA write and low-clock optimizations are enabled in normal_mode.
+	 * The RDSFDP (0x5A) command requires 8 dummy cycles and is sensitive to
+	 * timing variations that can cause 1-byte read offset corruption.
+	 */
+	if (op->cmd.opcode == 0x5A && op->data.dir == SPI_MEM_DATA_IN) {
+		dev_dbg(dev, "RDSFDP (0x5A) detected: routing to USER mode for stability\n");
+		return aspeed_spi_read_user(chip, op, op->addr.val,
+					    op->data.nbytes, op->data.buf.in);
+	}
+
 	addr_mode_reg = readl(aspi->regs + CE_CTRL_REG);
 	addr_mode_reg_backup = addr_mode_reg;
 	addr_data_mask = readl(aspi->regs + CMD_CTRL_REG);
